From 83e790022f03fb1e1715f1134e9831e868f92278 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:55:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Post-tail exit bound: unwind exit code, exit-diag
 record, funnel hand-back

Follow-up to PR #1949's review nits (t_01a1d3dde703d02f):

1. The shutdown tail runs in start_gateway's finally. When runner.stop() or
   wait_gateway_runtime raised, it still armed the bound with its verdict
   (maybe 0), while the escaping exception makes the process exit 1 (or the
   SystemExit's code). The tail now reads the active exception and arms the
   bound with that code.
2. A bound exit skips `hermes gateway run`'s asyncio.run.returned /
   gateway.exit_clean / nonzero_exit_record records. The watcher writes a
   gateway.post_tail_bound exit-diag record (warning: exit code, seconds
   over the target, target reason, phase marks) before taking the funnel.
3. When the bound's funnel raised, it handed the exit back by clearing
   exit_owner, but a main thread already parked in enter_exit_funnel waited
   on a private Event forever (only the hard deadline exited). The funnel
   now parks on a module _handback event that the watcher sets on failure,
   then retries the disarm.

Tests: tests/gateway/test_update_exit_target.py (unwind code for an
exception and SystemExit(75), record written before the funnel, parked
funnel wakes on hand-back) and tests/gateway/test_exit_deadline.py
(subprocess: a checkpointed stop with a wedged executor exits through the
bound with a gateway.post_tail_bound record). 5 new tests fail on base,
pass on head.
---
